# Liquid Syntax Essentials

## Core Syntax Rules

### Delimiters

- `{{ ... }}` - Output (prints value)
- `{{- ... -}}` - Output with whitespace trim
- `{% ... %}` - Logic tags (no output)
- `{%- ... -%}` - Logic tags with whitespace trim
- `{%- liquid ... -%}` - Multiline logic without delimiters

### 🛑 Critical Limitations (AI Agents: MEMORIZE THESE)

- **NO parentheses** in conditions - will cause syntax error
- **NO ternary operators** - use `{% if %}` blocks instead
- **NO more than 2 logical operators** - nest `if` statements for complex logic
- **Max 50 iterations** per `for` loop - use `paginate` or fail silently
- **Max 5 levels** of include/render nesting - plan component depth carefully

## Common Patterns

### Variable Assignment

```liquid
{%- liquid
  # Always use liquid tag for multiline logic
  assign product = product | default: null
  assign show_price = show_price | default: true
  assign classes = 'product-card' | append: ' ' | append: custom_class
-%}
```

### Conditional Rendering

```liquid
{%- if product and product.available -%}
  {{- product.title | escape -}}
{%- elsif product -%}
  {{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}
{%- endif -%}
```

### Safe Array Iteration

```liquid
{%- for item in collection.products limit: 20 -%}
  {{ item.title }}
{%- else -%}
  {{ 'collections.empty' | t }}
{%- endfor -%}
```

### Parameter Validation in Snippets

```liquid
{%- liquid
  assign product = product | default: blank
  unless product != blank
    echo '<!-- Error: product required -->'
    break
  endunless
-%}
```

## Shopify-Specific Tags

### Essential Theme Tags

- `{% render 'snippet-name' %}` - Include snippet (isolated scope)
- `{% section 'section-name' %}` - Static section
- `{% form 'product' %}` - Product form with required product context
- `{% paginate collection.products by 24 %}` - Handle large collections

### Form Types (require specific contexts)

```liquid
{% form 'product', product %}     <!-- Requires product -->
{% form 'cart', cart %}           <!-- Requires cart -->
{% form 'customer_login' %}       <!-- No context needed -->
{% form 'contact' %}              <!-- No context needed -->
```

## Filter Quick Patterns

### Most Common Filter Mistakes

```liquid
❌ WRONG (AI agents often try these):
{{ price | format_money }}           → Use: money
{{ product | product_img_url }}      → Use: image_url
{{ array | contains: object }}       → contains is an operator, not filter
{{ text | t: 'key' }}               → t filter takes key first: {{ 'key' | t }}

✅ CORRECT:
{{ price | money }}
{{ product | image_url: width: 300 }}
{% if array contains 'string' %}
{{ 'translation.key' | t }}
```

### Filter Type Checking

Before chaining filters, verify types match (see [Full Reference](mdc:.cursor/rules/lang-liquid-full-reference.mdc)):

```liquid
{{ 'text' | upcase }} → returns: string {{ 'text' | split: ' ' }} → returns:
array {{ array | first }} → returns: untyped
```

## Performance Patterns

### Efficient Liquid

```liquid
{%- liquid
  # Good: Single liquid tag for logic
  assign collection = collections[handle]
  assign products = collection.products
-%}

<!-- Bad: Multiple separate tags -->
{% assign collection = collections[handle] %}
{% assign products = collection.products %}
```

### Avoid Expensive Operations

```liquid
<!-- Bad: Iterating all products -->
{% for product in all_products %}

<!-- Good: Use paginated collection -->
{% paginate collection.products by 24 %}
  {% for product in collection.products %}
```

## ⚠️ Common AI Agent Mistakes

### 1. `contains` with Objects (ONLY Works with Strings)

```liquid
❌ {% if collection.products contains product %}
  <!-- FAILS: contains can't compare objects -->
{% endif %}

❌ {% if cart.items contains line_item %}
  <!-- FAILS: contains can't compare objects -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% assign product_ids = collection.products | map: 'id' %}
{% if product_ids contains product.id %}
  <!-- Works: comparing IDs (numbers converted to strings) -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if product.tags contains 'featured' %}
  <!-- Works: string array contains string -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if product.title contains 'Sale' %}
  <!-- Works: string contains substring -->
{% endif %}
```

### 2. Variable Scope Isolation

```liquid
❌ {% assign product_title = product.title %}
{% render 'card' %}
<!-- Inside card.liquid: product_title is undefined -->

✅ {% render 'card', product: product %}
<!-- Pass the entire object -->

✅ {% render 'card', title: product.title, price: product.price %}
<!-- Pass specific properties -->

❌ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {% render 'card' %}
  <!-- Inside card.liquid: product is undefined -->
{% endfor %}

✅ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {% render 'card', product: product %}
  <!-- Explicitly pass loop variable -->
{% endfor %}
```

### 3. Loop Indexing (Starts at 1, Not 0)

```liquid
{% for product in collection.products %}
  {{ forloop.index }}   <!-- 1, 2, 3, 4... (NOT 0, 1, 2, 3) -->
  {{ forloop.index0 }}  <!-- 0, 1, 2, 3... (zero-indexed) -->
  {{ forloop.first }}   <!-- true on first iteration -->
  {{ forloop.last }}    <!-- true on last iteration -->
{% endfor %}

❌ {% if forloop.index == 0 %}
  <!-- Never true! Use forloop.first or forloop.index0 == 0 -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if forloop.first %}
  <!-- Correct way to detect first iteration -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if forloop.index0 == 0 %}
  <!-- Also works for first iteration -->
{% endif %}
```

### 4. Null/Empty/Blank Checks

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  blank: checks for nil, false, empty string, or empty array/object
  empty: only checks for empty collections (arrays, strings)
  nil: only checks for undefined/null
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {% if product == nil %}
  <!-- Too narrow: misses empty strings, false -->
{% endif %}

❌ {% if product == empty %}
  <!-- Won't work for nil values -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if product == blank %}
  <!-- Best: catches nil, empty, false -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% unless product != blank %}
  <!-- Double negative: unless not blank = if blank -->
{% endunless %}

{%- comment -%} Real-world examples {%- endcomment -%}

✅ {% assign product = all_products[handle] | default: blank %}
{% if product != blank %}
  <!-- Product exists and has data -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if collection.products.size > 0 %}
  <!-- Explicit size check for arrays -->
{% else %}
  <!-- Collection is empty or nil -->
{% endif %}
```

### 5. Name Collisions (Local Variables Override Globals)

```liquid
❌ {%- assign product = 'featured' -%}
<!-- Now 'product' is a string, not the product object! -->
{% if product.available %}
  <!-- ERROR: Strings don't have 'available' property -->
{% endif %}

✅ {%- assign product_type = 'featured' -%}
<!-- Use different name to avoid collision -->
{% if product.available %}
  <!-- product object still accessible -->
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%} Common collision variables {%- endcomment -%}
Global objects that shouldn't be overridden:
- product, collection, cart, customer, shop
- page, blog, article, search
- template, section, block
- settings, localization, routes
```

### 6. Filter Chaining Type Mismatches

```liquid
❌ {{ product.title | split: ' ' | money }}
<!-- FAILS: money filter expects number, got array -->

❌ {{ product.price | upcase }}
<!-- FAILS: upcase expects string, got number -->

✅ {{ product.price | money | upcase }}
<!-- Works: money returns string, upcase processes string -->

✅ {{ product.title | split: ' ' | first | upcase }}
<!-- Works: first returns string, upcase processes string -->

{%- comment -%} Always check return types {%- endcomment -%}
{{ product.tags | join: ', ' | upcase }}
<!-- join returns string → upcase works ✅ -->

{{ collection.products | map: 'title' | join: ', ' }}
<!-- map returns array → join returns string ✅ -->
```

### 7. Array Access and Boundaries

```liquid
❌ {% assign first = collection.products.first %}
{% if first %}
  <!-- FAILS when array is empty: first is blank, not false -->
  {{ first.title }}
{% endif %}

✅ {% if collection.products.size > 0 %}
  {% assign first = collection.products.first %}
  {{ first.title }}
{% endif %}

✅ {% for product in collection.products limit: 1 %}
  {{ product.title }}
  <!-- Loop body only executes if array has items -->
{% endfor %}

❌ {% for i in (1..collection.products.size) %}
  {{ collection.products[i].title }}
  <!-- WRONG: arrays are 0-indexed, but range starts at 1 -->
{% endfor %}

✅ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {{ product.title }}
  <!-- Always prefer direct iteration -->
{% endfor %}
```

### 8. Attempting Complex Logic

```liquid
❌ {% if (product.available and product.price < 50) or (product.tags contains 'sale' and product.compare_at_price > 0) %}
  <!-- SYNTAX ERROR: parentheses not supported -->
{% endif %}

❌ {% if product.available ? 'In Stock' : 'Sold Out' %}
  <!-- SYNTAX ERROR: ternary operators not supported -->
{% endif %}

✅ {%- liquid
  assign is_cheap_available = false
  if product.available and product.price < 5000
    assign is_cheap_available = true
  endif

  assign is_on_sale = false
  if product.tags contains 'sale' and product.compare_at_price > 0
    assign is_on_sale = true
  endif
-%}

{% if is_cheap_available or is_on_sale %}
  <!-- Complex logic broken into manageable pieces -->
{% endif %}

✅ {%- liquid
  if product.available
    assign status = 'In Stock'
  else
    assign status = 'Sold Out'
  endif
-%}
{{ status }}
<!-- Manual ternary simulation -->
```

### 9. Forgetting Filter Argument Syntax

```liquid
❌ {{ product | image_url: 300 }}
<!-- Wrong: named parameter required -->

✅ {{ product | image_url: width: 300 }}
<!-- Correct: named parameter -->

❌ {{ product.price | money: 'USD' }}
<!-- Wrong: money doesn't accept currency parameter -->

✅ {{ product.price | money }}
<!-- Correct: uses shop's currency settings -->

❌ {{ 'translation.key' | t: count: 3, 'name': 'John' }}
<!-- Wrong: inconsistent parameter syntax -->

✅ {{ 'translation.key' | t: count: 3, name: 'John' }}
<!-- Correct: all named parameters, no quotes on keys -->
```

### 10. Silent Failures and Missing Error Handling

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  Liquid fails silently in many cases - validate inputs!
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }}
<!-- If featured_image is nil, outputs nothing (silent fail) -->

✅ {% if product.featured_image %}
  <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }}" alt="{{ product.title }}">
{% else %}
  <img src="{{ 'placeholder.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ product.title }}">
{% endif %}

❌ {{ collection.products.first.title }}
<!-- If collection.products is empty, silent fail -->

✅ {% if collection.products.size > 0 %}
  {{ collection.products.first.title }}
{% else %}
  {{ 'collections.empty' | t }}
{% endif %}

❌ {% for product in collections[handle].products %}
  <!-- If collection doesn't exist, loop silently skips -->
{% endfor %}

✅ {% assign collection = collections[handle] %}
{% if collection and collection.products.size > 0 %}
  {% for product in collection.products %}
    {{ product.title }}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  {{ 'collections.not_found' | t }}
{% endif %}
```

## Edge Cases and Type Coercion

### Price and Money Handling

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  Prices in Shopify are in cents (integer)
  100 = $1.00, 1999 = $19.99
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {% if product.price > 50 %}
  <!-- WRONG: comparing cents to dollars (50 cents, not $50) -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if product.price > 5000 %}
  <!-- Correct: 5000 cents = $50.00 -->
{% endif %}

❌ {{ product.price / 100 }}
  <!-- Wrong: displays "19.99" instead of "$19.99" -->

✅ {{ product.price | money }}
  <!-- Correct: displays "$19.99" with currency -->

{%- comment -%}
  Comparing prices: always compare raw values
{%- endcomment -%}

✅ {% if product.compare_at_price > product.price %}
  <span class="sale-badge">Sale</span>
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  Calculate discount percentage
{%- endcomment -%}

✅ {%- liquid
  assign difference = product.compare_at_price | minus: product.price
  assign discount = difference | times: 100 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price
-%}
Save {{ discount }}%
```

### Number Type Coercion

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  Liquid converts types unpredictably in some contexts
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {% assign quantity = '5' %}
{% if quantity > 3 %}
  <!-- May work, but unreliable string-to-number coercion -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% assign quantity = 5 %}
<!-- Or use filter to ensure number -->
{% assign quantity = '5' | plus: 0 %}
{% if quantity > 3 %}
  <!-- Reliable: explicit number -->
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  String concatenation vs. math
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {{ '10' | plus: '5' }}
  <!-- Outputs: 15 (coerced to numbers) -->

❌ {{ 'Price: ' | append: 10 }}
  <!-- Outputs: Price: 10 (number coerced to string) -->

✅ {{ 'Price: ' | append: product.price | append: ' USD' }}
  <!-- Explicit string concatenation -->
```

### Boolean Context Gotchas

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  Truthy values: everything except false, nil, blank
  Falsy values: false, nil, blank (empty string/array/object)
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {% if product.available == true %}
  <!-- Redundant: available is already boolean -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% if product.available %}
  <!-- Cleaner: direct boolean check -->
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  String '0' and 'false' are truthy!
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ {% assign enabled = 'false' %}
{% if enabled %}
  <!-- This IS TRUE! String 'false' is truthy -->
{% endif %}

✅ {% assign enabled = false %}
<!-- Or use comparison -->
{% if enabled == false or enabled == 'false' %}
  <!-- Explicit check -->
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  Empty arrays and objects
{%- endcomment -%}

✅ {% if collection.products.size > 0 %}
  <!-- Explicit: check size, not truthiness -->
{% endif %}

❌ {% if collection.products %}
  <!-- Empty array is still truthy! Always check size -->
{% endif %}
```

## Advanced Performance Patterns

### Minimize Object Property Access

```liquid
❌ {% for product in collection.products %}
  <h3>{{ product.title }}</h3>
  <p>{{ product.title | upcase }}</p>
  <span>{{ product.title | truncate: 20 }}</span>
  <!-- Accessing product.title 3 times -->
{% endfor %}

✅ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {% assign title = product.title %}
  <h3>{{ title }}</h3>
  <p>{{ title | upcase }}</p>
  <span>{{ title | truncate: 20 }}</span>
  <!-- Cache in variable: access once, use many times -->
{% endfor %}
```

### Avoid Nested Loops with Large Datasets

```liquid
❌ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {% for variant in product.variants %}
    {% for tag in product.tags %}
      <!-- Triple nested loop: O(n³) complexity -->
    {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

✅ {% for product in collection.products limit: 20 %}
  <!-- Limit outer loop -->
  {% assign variant_count = product.variants.size | at_most: 5 %}
  {% for variant in product.variants limit: variant_count %}
    <!-- Process only what's needed -->
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

✅ Use paginate for large collections
{% paginate collection.products by 24 %}
  {% for product in collection.products %}
    <!-- Pagination prevents timeout -->
  {% endfor %}
{% endpaginate %}
```

### Conditional Rendering vs. CSS Display

```liquid
❌ <div style="{% unless show_banner %}display: none;{% endunless %}">
  {% render 'expensive-banner', products: collection.products %}
  <!-- Snippet still executes even when hidden! -->
</div>

✅ {% if show_banner %}
  <div>
    {% render 'expensive-banner', products: collection.products %}
    <!-- Only executes when needed -->
  </div>
{% endif %}
```

### Reduce Filter Chains

```liquid
❌ {{ product.title | upcase | strip | truncate: 50 | escape }}
<!-- 4 filter operations -->

✅ {% assign title = product.title | strip | truncate: 50 %}
{{ title | escape }}
<!-- Split when reusing intermediate results -->

{%- comment -%}
  Some filters are expensive - cache results
{%- endcomment -%}

❌ <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }}">
<img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }}" loading="lazy">
<!-- image_url called twice -->

✅ {% assign image_url = product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 %}
<img src="{{ image_url }}">
<img src="{{ image_url }}" loading="lazy">
```

## Metafields and Dynamic Content

### Safe Metafield Access

```liquid
❌ {{ product.metafields.custom.subtitle }}
<!-- Silent fail if namespace or key doesn't exist -->

✅ {% if product.metafields.custom.subtitle != blank %}
  <p class="subtitle">{{ product.metafields.custom.subtitle }}</p>
{% endif %}

✅ {% assign subtitle = product.metafields.custom.subtitle | default: 'Default subtitle' %}
<p class="subtitle">{{ subtitle }}</p>

{%- comment -%}
  Metafield value types (use metafield_tag or metafield_text for auto-formatting)
{%- endcomment -%}

✅ {{ product.metafields.custom.description | metafield_text }}
<!-- Handles different value types correctly -->

✅ {{ product.metafields.custom.specs | metafield_tag }}
<!-- Renders with proper HTML structure -->
```

### Dynamic Object Access

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  Bracket notation for dynamic property access
{%- endcomment -%}

✅ {% assign field_name = 'title' %}
{{ product[field_name] }}
<!-- Dynamically access product.title -->

✅ {% for field in 'title,price,vendor' | split: ',' %}
  <dt>{{ field | capitalize }}</dt>
  <dd>{{ product[field] }}</dd>
{% endfor %}

✅ {% assign collection_handle = 'featured' %}
{% assign collection = collections[collection_handle] %}
<!-- Dynamic collection lookup -->

❌ {% assign product = all_products.{{ handle }} %}
<!-- WRONG: can't use interpolation in dot notation -->

✅ {% assign product = all_products[handle] %}
<!-- Correct: bracket notation -->
```

## Whitespace Control Patterns

### Strategic Whitespace Trimming

```liquid
❌ {%- for product in collection.products -%}
  {%- assign title = product.title -%}
  {{- title -}}
{%- endfor -%}
<!-- Over-aggressive: removes all whitespace -->
Output: ProductAProductBProductC

✅ {% for product in collection.products %}
  {%- assign title = product.title -%}
  {{ title }}
{% endfor %}
<!-- Preserves necessary whitespace between items -->
Output:
  Product A
  Product B
  Product C

✅ {%- for product in collection.products -%}
  {{ product.title }}{{ unless forloop.last }}, {% endunless %}
{%- endfor -%}
<!-- Clean comma-separated list -->
Output: Product A, Product B, Product C
```

### Inline vs. Block Liquid Tags

```liquid
❌ {% liquid
assign total = 0
for item in cart.items
  assign total = total | plus: item.line_price
endfor
%}
<!-- Hard to read, hard to debug -->

✅ {%- liquid
  # Better: Use liquid tag for short, related operations
  assign has_sale_items = false
  assign has_preorder_items = false

  for item in cart.items
    if item.product.tags contains 'sale'
      assign has_sale_items = true
    endif
    if item.product.tags contains 'preorder'
      assign has_preorder_items = true
    endif
  endfor
-%}

✅ Use separate tags for complex, unrelated logic
{% assign shipping_threshold = 5000 %}

{% if cart.total_price >= shipping_threshold %}
  {% assign free_shipping = true %}
{% endif %}

{% for item in cart.items %}
  <!-- Complex loop body -->
{% endfor %}
```

